      "writtenOn": "2016-12-13T02:11:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider breaking up the subsections of the test, with vertical whitespace, to make the test easier to skim. I think a reasonable way to do this is to have some whitespace after each Arrange-Act-Assert sequence. (See go/unit-test-practices#structure for the idea behind the sequences.)\n\nHere, that would be something like:\n\n\n  configureChip(...);\n  //...\n\n\n  sp\u003cIWifiApIface\u003e iface;\n  // ...\n\n\n  std::string iface_name \u003d ...;\n  // ...\n\n\n  EXPECT_EQ(removeApIface(...));\n  // ...\n\nSame suggestion for other tests that have multiple AAA sequences.",
      "revId": "75b8e705a64b4b81d1b64f91c2b7d88ff4bff19f",
